                    <h3>What is a Bond?</h3>
                    <p>
                        A Bond is a type of investment where an investor lends money to a company, government, or other eligible issuer for a specific period. In return, the bond may provide interest payments and repayment of the principal amount according to its terms.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Provides a defined investment period or maturity date.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>May provide regular interest payments based on the bond terms.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Different bonds have different levels of risk, return, and credit quality.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Can be considered as part of a diversified investment portfolio.</span></li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Bonds can be considered by investors who are looking to add debt investments to their overall financial plan. They may be used for income planning, portfolio diversification, or other financial objectives depending on the type of bond and its terms.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Before investing in a Bond, consider the issuer's credit quality, interest rate, maturity period, repayment terms, liquidity, market conditions, taxation, and associated risks. Bond prices and returns can change depending on interest rates, credit conditions, and other market factors.
                    </p>
